<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:24Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel votes in first election since October 7 attack as Netanyahu faces crucial test</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b93221df97186b58ea70176e371b2c6adc8465b232b3e02748c30d8c7fd43be</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T04:12:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-2026-netanyahu-october-7--393517cfbc4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-2026-netanyahu-october-7" /><summary type="html">Israelis head to the polls on Tuesday for the first time since Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack, in a closely contested election seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. The vote follows three years of regional wars, with Netanyahu running neck and neck with centrist rival Gadi Eisenkot.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Mecca pact nations hold talks with Iran to prevent renewed Middle East war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33530430b49574d1ae3e0fe77401471b9778609bab34dc300fc896f929174a2b</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:24:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-iran-talks-mecca-pact-nations-war--271d84436965.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-iran-talks-mecca-pact-nations-war" /><summary type="html">Senior officials from Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan held talks in Iran on Monday aimed at preventing renewed fighting in the Middle East, with Tehran describing discussions as “very good”. The diplomatic push, attended by Saudi Defence Minister Prince Khalid bin Salman, followed warnings from Washington, Tehran and Israel of renewed hostilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UN cites 'ethnic cleansing' concerns around Israel's Palestinian displacement operation in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f63c1f841e7cdb99a9b115bc3baa68cbf88504acebb9f0611b905030c42c4b4</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:59:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron--f54dc7b36717.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron" /><summary type="html">The United Nations on Monday raised "ethnic cleansing" concerns following Israel's operation to displace by force more than 3,000 Palestinians from their homes in Hebron in the West Bank after two Palestinian gunmen killed two Israeli soldiers at a checkpoint near the city on Friday. UN rights chief Volker Turk said in a statement that the "aggressive operation" must end, and that "collective punishment is a grave violation of international law".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Opponents accuse Netanyahu of stoking tensions with Iran before Israel's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:724fce2e8a856e1d5d73fbb0c056ffb087b3d3aff487d5e1b5daafaba6e27fe6</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:11:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election--5429441497ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's defence minister denied on Monday (October 26) reports of a rift between PM Netanyahu and the army over Iran, before the vote.  Netanyahu has campaigned heavily on his security credentials, insisting only he can "finish the job" in the US-Israeli war on Iran. His main rival, ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot, has accused him of playing up the Iran threat when it suits him politically, and of failing to accomplish his war goals. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli candidate Eisenkot pledges to unite country as Netanyahu deems him 'soft' on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cda5e778a2d36402e000c353bc68fb2b26da746121316bd5541fa56dde68e4a4</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:58:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran--bd8634a89185.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Israeli presidential candidate Gadi Eisenkot's pledge made Sunday to "heal" Israeli society after Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's divisive tenure resonated with some voters attending his final campaign rally before polling begins Tuesday. Netanyahu meanwhile received fresh backing for re-election from US President Donald Trump and deemed Eisenkot "soft" on Iran.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel election: unable to vote from abroad, expats have to fly home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f2cccb1dc4b2f0ef06f6c85c54e56dad509e1f0b24812e8e7d16901742f6bc3</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:47:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home--cdb70f36234d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home" /><summary type="html">Israelis can’t vote from abroad, so tens of thousands of expats are expected to fly home for the election. At Tel Aviv airport, supporters of opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot are already waiting at arrivals. A “Fly and Vote” initiative helps expats organise their trip, despite a failed petition from Netanyahu’s Likud party to restrict it. With polls predicting a tight race, every vote could count, and the result will decide the Prime Minister’s fate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Jordan's strikes on Syria over church terror attack kill several civilians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf8921329ae8f17679b36fe9bae6a467b06e98afa4bd9743f4f5c8582c31fdd0</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:12:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church--ff7fe6210ee5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church" /><summary type="html">Jordanian authorities on Monday arrested three suspects over last week's terror attack that killed nine people in a church funeral procession in the village of Hammoud. Jordan's military later launched strikes on "terrorist organisations" in neighbouring Syria in retaliation for the attack by alleged Islamic extremists, killing at least eight civilians including women and children, a health official said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands of Israelis living abroad expected to fly in for pivotal vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0e00b463b9434b494dbdda080ae2a452a561df6b0755119fa79e0e40e359dd1</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:20:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote--a3d6b8696ede.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27). Unable to vote from abroad, tens of thousands of expatriate citizens have been flying in from across the world to cast their ballots. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky met some of them at the airport.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Netanyahu's security promise win him this election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e4db50e9915c5c1d14d2342b10d0288a03330d02b254aa0e72b29b350c48acc</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election--7245e677289a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election" /><summary type="html">Since the beginning of his political career, Benjamin Netanyahu, Israel's longest-serving prime minister, has campaigned on a promise that he is the only one who will keep the Jewish state safe. As Israelis head to the polls for their first election since the October7 Hamas attacks and the start of the war in Gaza, Netanyahu's strategy might be less effective. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel braces for national elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcb12a8f45892b4d2a02d6a956ef0516843c9c640f540516cb95dc160aa9c439</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:35:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu--603ad1ac5180.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27)  in the first elections since the October 7th attacks in 2023. Unable to vote abroad, expatriate citizens have been flying in from around the world to participate in a vote widely seen as being a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Arab Israeli voters could prove decisive in the upcoming elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7db3333c3465dfd0bba35cb8ee6e3679be3ab7c31989b8a6095d41bbd0cb167c</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:13:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections--cf7c16524fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections" /><summary type="html">In Israel’s election the vote of Arab Israeli citizens could be crucial for the outcome and fate of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu who is standing for re-election. Traditionally voting turnout is lower among Arab Israelis than among the rest of the population. But this time some feel it’s their duty more than ever to cast their ballot given the policies and wars undertaken by Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>A look at the main issues in Israeli elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e191088ed8e9eb937ba979d54ab60798bbeab1381bfe3fec10edaa990f17432</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:19:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:59:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu--91568101be2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis will vote Tuesday (October 27) in the first national elections since Hamas' Oct. 7, 2023, attack in what is widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership. He rejected ICC war crimes claims and denied corruption as national elections approach. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election seen as a referendum: For or against Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0af5732e28e4f847004712c0e15aa567860996e9523d0ac60326fe55f58ca5f</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:40:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu--842384761d07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has led his country almost continuously for nearly 17 years. But will he manage to retain power following Tuesday's election? Netanyahu's latest term has divided Israeli society more than ever and will be marked by the October 7 attacks, his handling of the conflicts in Gaza, Iran and Lebanon, as well as his controversial judicial reform. FRANCE 24's David Gilberg reports, with Lauren Bain.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Report: IDF chief pushes back on Netanyahu's order</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d2beb377825be5d62a8171b2abc420b0bb2cbb38282448d2c7ea0ca9d448f89</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T23:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261025-report-idf-pushes-back-on-netanyahu-s-order--18329c3cde80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261025-report-idf-pushes-back-on-netanyahu-s-order" /><summary type="html">An extraordinary confrontation at the top of Israel's leadership, just two days before the election. Israeli media report Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and military chief Eyal Zamir are at odds over Iran. Zamir reportedly fears government instructions could trigger an immediate military escalation and has demanded written authorisation. Netanyahu denies any confrontation. The reports come as he warns Iran could attack Israel to disrupt Tuesday's vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Demonstrators rally against government ahead of election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6521a29606b417b22c5935c3bacfc25e824391d0210c89af005c47b0dce59da</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:38:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election--605d00c22edc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election" /><summary type="html">In Israel, the anti-Netanyahu movement is mobilising. Thousands gathered in Tel Aviv on Friday to protest against the Israeli government, just three days ahead of a general election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Families forcibly displaced in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57612e45304ac41a7d4a7a4ad7622fa4ad4ce6b57d92608f7cf7a2e04071b273</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:35:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron--c0b8d6b2a6c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron" /><summary type="html">More Palestinian families have been displaced in the occupied West Bank as Israeli forces continue operations in Hebron, following a deadly shooting that killed two Israeli soldiers on Friday. With elections scheduled for Tuesday, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has vowed a heavy response to the attack. Morgaene Ayre has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands take to Tel Aviv's streets for protests against Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2959af4cb0f67595cde5674f4417c8c9dd4ea8f3f7c6861fabf7112c2714b89</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T18:21:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu--99da939090a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Thousands marched against Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government in Tel Aviv on Saturday – just three days before Israel's general election – demanding accountability for the failure to prevent a Hamas-led attack on October 7, 2023, which led to the war in Gaza.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthi rebels claim new attacks on oil facilities and airports across Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b038101578ddc4efebaacfb39086c892c4e11e46555d04e0c0dd9e1e9d8f73dc</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:50:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia--98ea10f02978.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-yemen-s-houthi-rebels-claim-new-attacks-on-oil-facilities-and-airports-across-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Iran-allied Houthi rebels said they launched attacks at Saudi oil facilities and airports on Saturday while Yemen’s Saudi-backed government ​said the ‌group also fired three ballistic missiles at coast guard sites in ⁠the port city of Aden.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel begins demolitions in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:598d69477632fc02067a0ddfcc8cc6c658285128a72bfb9f367bc650304ba946</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T17:13:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-begins-demolitions-in-west-bank--1cdd8864f331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-begins-demolitions-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">The Palestinian Authority has called for international pressure on Israel after a Palestinian official said around 1,200 Palestinians in Hebron in the West Bank were forced to leave their homes following an attack on Friday which killed two Israeli soldiers. The head of Hebron's municipality said an additional 1,300 may also be forced to leave.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel to close all West Bank land crossings on election day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe45bc6a82bc8c79cb0dea76cdbc690df903e6c7062a1b920d86361c0397d100</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T13:52:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israel-to-close-all-land-crossings-with-west-bank-on-election-day--97f1a94dfee6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israel-to-close-all-land-crossings-with-west-bank-on-election-day" /><summary type="html">Israel announced it would be closing all land crossings with the West Bank on the day of next week's parliamentary elections. The measure comes as Israel conducts a large-scale operation in the occupied Palestinian territory and 2,000 residents of Hebron have been displaced from their homes after Palestinian gunmen killed two soldiers in the area.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli forces displace 2,000 Palestinians in Hebron after deadly attack on soldiers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19542cf89b8c284264680d48ae4ebffcf43cb8ef665207e74e30b35bc07e8341</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T13:50:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israeli-forces-displace-1-200-palestinians-in-hebron-after-deadly-attack-on-soldiers--bcc1afec2ab7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-israeli-forces-displace-1-200-palestinians-in-hebron-after-deadly-attack-on-soldiers" /><summary type="html">The Palestinian Authority called for international pressure on Israel after a Palestinian official said around 1,200 Palestinians in Hebron in the West Bank were forced to leave their homes following an attack on Friday which killed two Israeli soldiers. Israeli defence minister Israel Katz later confirmed in an interview that the displacements had reached the 2,000 mark.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu orders West Bank operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9a7acade11e01a1f9026dc581712ea37999a98947dcc6476fe6f83db87a968f</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-orders-west-bank-operation--93ec6832b46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-orders-west-bank-operation" /><summary type="html">Israel has imposed widespread closures across the occupied West Bank and displaced residents following attacks by Palestinian gunmen that killed two Israeli soldiers. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu visited the site of the attack near Hebron and instructed security forces to immediately cordon off the city. Morgan Ayre reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu weighs West Bank operation ahead of elections: ‘Politically, it will not help anybody’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f62d8d8da4d8a1f7cacf45f61c188a1329c7b129a8391f7cc387919f1b16e83c</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T18:26:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261023-netanyahu-weighs-west-bank-operation-ahead-of-elections-politically-it-will-not-help-anybod--82f68804f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261023-netanyahu-weighs-west-bank-operation-ahead-of-elections-politically-it-will-not-help-anybody" /><summary type="html">As Israel approaches a consequential parliamentary election amid renewed violence in the occupied West Bank, Yedioth Ahronoth Senior Journalist Ben-Dror Yemini offers a critical assessment of Benjamin Netanyahu's political prospects, the limits of military escalation and the shifting relationship between national security and electoral legitimacy.
 
Since October 7, 2023 "Netanyahu is not popular anymore," Yemini argues, identifying the Hamas-led attacks as a decisive turning point in the Israeli prime minister's public standing.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>How Israeli settlers wearing keffiyehs are attacking West Bank olive groves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b4ac8c4a0730694583f7c560d0fcbf24d62c8eab377dd7dc98874f814404c13</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-how-israeli-settlers-wearing-keffiyehs-are-attacking-west-bank-olive-groves--10563b4076b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-how-israeli-settlers-wearing-keffiyehs-are-attacking-west-bank-olive-groves" /><summary type="html">The olive harvest officially began in the West Bank on October 15, 2026, and it has coincided with an uptick in violence towards Palestinians carried out by both Israeli settlers and soldiers. Meanwhile, the settlers and soldiers have been using social media to promote an aesthetic, Instagram-friendly and nationalistic view of these harvests.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: Could Arab parties play kingmaker in the next Knesset ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5af91c7176096622a5ccd3db93ae541f0211d07aec9ba62ca975f21a5661296</id><updated>2026-10-27T05:17:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T17:11:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-could-arab-parties-play-kingmaker-in-the-next-knesset--cd40bcd2e863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-could-arab-parties-play-kingmaker-in-the-next-knesset" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls for the first legislative election since Hamas's October 7 attacks, neither Prime Minister Benjamin #Netanyahu's Likud party nor former army chief 